===== baumkuchen (no command) --help =====
baumkuchen — a blog that carries the same idea at up to five lengths

Usage:
  baumkuchen [serve] [folder] [flags]
  baumkuchen build [folder] [flags]
  baumkuchen bundle [folder] --out FILE
  baumkuchen check [folder] [flags]
  baumkuchen init [folder] [flags]
  baumkuchen version
  baumkuchen help [command]

Commands:
  serve    serve the posts, live (the command that stands in for the others)
  build    write the static site, then stop
  bundle   write one file with the program and the posts inside it
  check    say what is wrong with the posts
  init     write the settings file for a new site
  version  say which build this is
  help     show this help and stop

Global flags:
  --config PATH          the settings file to read
  -q, --quiet            say nothing but the result
  -h, --help             show this help and stop

The folder is the one with the markdown in it. It may come before or after
the flags. A folder whose name is the name of a command is written with a
path in front of it, as in ./build.

Run "baumkuchen <command> --help" for the flags of one command.
===== baumkuchen serve --help =====
baumkuchen serve — serve the posts, live (the command that stands in for the others)

Usage:
  baumkuchen serve [folder] [flags]

Flags:
  --addr ADDR            the address to listen on
  --open                 open the site in a browser
  --drafts               show the drafts, wherever it listens
  --no-drafts            hide the drafts, even on the loopback address
  --dev                  read the templates and the stylesheet from disk, and show every error
  --title TEXT           the name of the site
  --heading TEXT         the line under the wordmark
  --favicon PATH         the picture on the tab

Global flags:
  --config PATH          the settings file to read
  -q, --quiet            say nothing but the result
  -h, --help             show this help and stop
===== baumkuchen build --help =====
baumkuchen build — write the static site, then stop

Usage:
  baumkuchen build [folder] [flags]

Flags:
  -o, --out DIR          the folder to write the site into
  --base PATH            the folder the site is published in
  --clean                remove the files of an earlier build first
  --drafts               put the drafts in the built site
  --title TEXT           the name of the site
  --heading TEXT         the line under the wordmark
  --favicon PATH         the picture on the tab

Global flags:
  --config PATH          the settings file to read
  -q, --quiet            say nothing but the result
  -h, --help             show this help and stop
===== baumkuchen bundle --help =====
baumkuchen bundle — write one file with the program and the posts inside it

Usage:
  baumkuchen bundle [folder] --out FILE

Flags:
  -o, --out FILE         the file to write

Global flags:
  --config PATH          the settings file to read
  -q, --quiet            say nothing but the result
  -h, --help             show this help and stop
===== baumkuchen check --help =====
baumkuchen check — say what is wrong with the posts

Usage:
  baumkuchen check [folder] [flags]

Flags:
  --json                 give the report as JSON
  --strict               stop with 1 when there is a warning

Global flags:
  --config PATH          the settings file to read
  -q, --quiet            say nothing but the result
  -h, --help             show this help and stop
===== baumkuchen init --help =====
baumkuchen init — write the settings file for a new site

Usage:
  baumkuchen init [folder] [flags]

Flags:
  --force                write over a settings file that is already there

Global flags:
  --config PATH          the settings file to read
  -q, --quiet            say nothing but the result
  -h, --help             show this help and stop
===== baumkuchen version --help =====
baumkuchen version — say which build this is

Usage:
  baumkuchen version

Flags:

Global flags:
  --config PATH          the settings file to read
  -q, --quiet            say nothing but the result
  -h, --help             show this help and stop
